<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A mesh system uses coordinated nodes, but each node still needs a useful location and a connection back to the rest of the network. More nodes do not automatically mean better speed or fewer dropouts.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="layout"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Map the useful locations</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Record the main router, the rooms and floors that need coverage, thick walls or other construction between them, and the devices and tasks that matter. Include the room where the connection is already useful so it can be compared with the difficult area.</p>
